WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
Hey, welcome to Planetarian Daily, episode 101.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.760
Today is June 25th, 2026.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.900
Here's what's new in science, health,

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.220
and longevity research.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.000
AI analysis of ECG recordings identified

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
a new marker tied to sudden cardiac death risk

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.500
across three cohorts.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.540
Deep learning applied to standard ECGs

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.660
uncovered a previously unrecognized electrical pattern

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.780
associated with elevated sudden cardiac death risk.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.560
The marker was validated in three independent cohorts

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.960
and correlated with benefit from implantable defibrillators.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.800
Researchers traced the signal to specific

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.860
ventricular conduction properties

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.420
rather than conventional QT or QRS measures.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.340
The work demonstrates how large scale wave form analysis

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.980
can surface subtle predictors

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.920
missed by traditional interpretation.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.240
Follow-up studies are examining whether the marker

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.200
can guide earlier device placement

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.740
and at-risk individuals.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.760
The Planetarian spotlight looks at how this ECG marker

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.720
adds a practical layer to cardiovascular risk stratification.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.980
Because the signal is extracted

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.840
from routine ECGs already collected in clinics,

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.980
it could be deployed without new hardware

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.320
or invasive testing.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.060
It moves the field closer to identifying

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.440
defibrillator candidates earlier in the disease course.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.860
What remains unclear is how the marker performs

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.860
in diverse ancestries and whether it changes

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:26.980
with common medications.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.000
How might routine ECG screening incorporate this pattern

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.080
once independent validation is complete?

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.260
Now, shifting to another internal system

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.000
that leaves measurable traces of disease risk.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.780
This time in the gut.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.560
An international team pooled metagenomic data

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.780
from multiple cohorts to identify a consistent microbial pattern

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.740
that tracks with elevated colon cancer risk.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.740
The signature includes depletion of fiber fermenting taxa

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.740
and enrichment of certain pro-inflammatory species.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.960
Higher dietary fiber intake was associated

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.440
with lower abundance of the risk associated taxa.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.880
The analysis strengthens evidence

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.520
that microbiome composition can serve

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.780
as a modifiable risk indicator.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.080
Next steps include prospective studies testing

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.020
whether targeted fiber interventions

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:20.980
shift the signature and alter cancer incidence.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.220
While microbial patterns reflect long-term dietary exposure,

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.820
a different environmental factor appears

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:30.420
to alter cellular aging clocks directly.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.040
Reduced oxygen exposure, including at high altitude,

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:37.360
produced measurable increases in epigenetic age

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.120
in both mouse tissues and human blood samples.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.460
The changes tracked with duration

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:46.500
and severity of hypoxia rather than chronological age alone.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.860
Researchers note the effect appears reversible

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.220
upon return to normal oxygen levels,

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.120
opening questions about recovery mechanisms.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.980
This finding adds environmental oxygen history

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:02.020
to the list of factors that can shift epigenetic clocks.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.300
Ongoing work is testing whether controlled re-oxygenation

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.760
protocols can accelerate reversal and affected individuals.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.740
Environmental conditions can shift molecular aging markers.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.000
The heart's own rhythm, meanwhile,

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.700
continuously tunes how the brain registers

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.940
the outside world.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.980
Cardiac cycle phase modulates neural responses

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.060
to incoming stimuli with certain phases

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.660
enhancing detection and others suppressing it.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:33.200
The effect occurs through barrel receptor feedback

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.500
that briefly alters cortical excitability.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:40.960
Researchers recorded simultaneous ECG and EEG

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.880
during visual and auditory tasks to map the relationship.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:49.900
The finding shows the heart continuously shapes perceptual thresholds

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.700
rather than serving only as a passive signal source.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.640
Future experiments will test whether cardiac locked stimulation

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.020
can improve sensory training protocols.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.740
Most people assume the brain processes incoming sites

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.660
and sounds on its own schedule,

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.980
independent of the rest of the body.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:10.660
In reality, the heart's rhythm continuously adjusts

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.460
neural sensitivity through barrel receptor signals

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.800
that reach the brainstem and cortex.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.280
Right now, as you listen, each heartbeat creates a brief window

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.140
of altered excitability, roughly every second.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:28.160
A single nerve impulse can travel at 120 meters per second,

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.280
yet the cardiac cycle modulates whether that impulse registers

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.380
as strongly as the one before it.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:39.000
Studies show detection thresholds can shift by 10 to 20%,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.780
depending on the phase of the heartbeat.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.080
The practical takeaway is that tasks requiring

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.740
fine sensory discrimination may benefit from alignment

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:48.800
with your own pulse.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.820
Simple pulse oximeter apps already let anyone test

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:55.540
whether performance varies across their cardiac cycle.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.500
Cellular self-organization operates

00:04:58.500 --> 00:04:59.880
without external direction.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.680
Japanese researchers identified mobile protein assemblies

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:06.900
called spet tap proteins that treadmill along

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.400
active networks without external cues.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.660
These filaments push the membrane outward at random sites,

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.640
generating protrusions that collectively determine

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.300
overall cell morphology.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.300
The mechanism explains how cells can reorganize their shape

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.380
in the absence of external signals.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.060
Experiments disrupting spTA formation

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.140
prevented spontaneous protrusions

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:33.020
while leaving stimulus driven shape changes intact.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.840
The work provides a new physical model

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:38.260
for studying cell polarity and migration.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.140
At larger scales, gate changes in aging dogs

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:44.580
may similarly reveal internal decline

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.140
before other signs appear.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.320
Veterinary researchers measured gate parameters

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:53.000
in senior dogs and found that reduced front leg stride length

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.300
tracked with poorer performance on cognitive tests.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:59.520
Hind leg stride showed no such relationship

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:03.220
and chronological age alone was a weak predictor.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.500
The pattern mirrors documented changes in humans

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.240
with dementia.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:10.060
The study proposes stride analysis

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.640
as a simple non-invasive screening tool

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.640
for canine cognitive dysfunction.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.220
Larger longitudinal cohorts are now being assembled

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.380
to determine how early the change appears

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.920
relative to other symptoms.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:26.240
Non-invasive markers of decline are valuable across species.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.800
Engineering proteins are now extending

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.020
what we can observe non-invasively inside living tissues.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.500
An international group, including David Baker's lab,

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.000
designed fluorescent proteins optimized

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.080
for shortwave infrared emission.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.860
The proteins were tested in mouse models

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.500
and produced clearer signals from deeper tissues

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.800
than previous probes.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.140
Computational redesign focused on stabilizing

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:53.100
the cromophore environment to shift emission spectra.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.480
The advanced supports non-invasive imaging

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:59.600
of internal structures without ionizing radiation.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.200
Next applications include tracking tumor margins

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.260
and monitoring transplanted cells

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:06.380
in larger animals.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:11.140
A separate population study found the organoclorine pesticide

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:14.160
chlorodicone in 80% of adults decades

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.420
after its agricultural use ended.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.380
Blood levels remain detectable across multiple perishes,

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:23.220
indicating long-term environmental persistence.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.480
Exposure routes include contaminated soil,

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.600
water, and locally grown food.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.320
The findings underscore the need for continued

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:35.340
biomonitoring in regions with historical pesticide application.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.100
Public health agencies are evaluating

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:41.140
whether dietary advisories should be updated.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:44.580
Reduced bone mineral density often progresses

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.100
without symptoms until a fracture occurs.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.360
Contributing factors include hormonal shifts,

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.240
inadequate calcium and vitamin D intake,

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.260
and prolonged inactivity.

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:58.380
Weight-bearing exercise and targeted nutrition

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:00.720
can slow loss and, in some cases,

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.040
produce modest density gains.

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:06.980
Screening via DEXA remains the primary detection method.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.100
The report emphasizes that early identification

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:13.860
allows intervention before progression to osteoporosis.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:17.220
Researchers tracked teen scrolling behavior

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.840
after Australia's nationwide restriction

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.000
and found little measurable change

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.300
in overall time spent on platforms.

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.220
Self-reported access through workarounds

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:29.380
or parental accounts remain common.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:33.380
The evaluation provides one of the first real-world assessments

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.520
of age-based platform bands.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:39.320
Data collection continues to determine whether effects emerge

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:41.860
over longer periods or vary by region.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:46.460
A new analysis links periodic changes in Earth's orbital dynamics

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:50.400
to clusters of extinction events across the phanerozoic.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:53.700
The model suggests tidal stresses on the crust

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:55.880
and mantle could trigger vulcanism

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.780
or seismic activity at critical intervals.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:02.440
The hypothesis integrates palantological records

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:04.600
with celestial mechanics calculations.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:07.780
It remains one of several proposed drivers

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:11.140
and will be tested against additional geological data sets.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:15.660
Two newly characterized, giant planets show radii

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.320
far larger than expected for their masses,

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.860
yielding densities below 0.1 grams per cubic centimeter.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:28.420
Transit and radial velocity data from multiple observatories

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.160
confirm the extreme properties.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:34.120
The findings challenge current models of gas giant formation

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:35.760
and atmospheric inflation.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:39.120
Follow-up atmospheric spectroscopy is planned

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:42.120
to determine the composition responsible for the low density.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:45.440
Observations captured characteristic distortions

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:47.180
in light and gravitational waves

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:50.760
consistent with the theoretical boundary of a black hole.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:54.160
The signals match predictions from general relativity

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.380
for photon rings and shadow features.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:00.340
The detection relied on coordinated data from radio arrays

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.720
and gravitational wave observatories.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:05.900
Confirmations strengthens the empirical basis

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:07.600
for horizon scale physics.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.900
Additional events are being analyzed for consistency.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:14.560
Case studies from six Pacific regions demonstrate

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:18.500
that traditional accounts accurately describe eruption sequences,

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:21.400
deposit locations, and recurrence intervals

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:22.980
spanning thousands of years.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.620
Integration with geological mapping

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:28.440
improved hazard models for several volcanoes.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:32.040
The approach shows how non-instrumental records

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.220
can extend observational baselines.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:37.900
Researchers are now cataloging additional traditions

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.580
for cross-validation with stratigraphic data.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:45.300
The same protein engineering effort that produced square emitters

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:48.540
also yielded variants with improved photo stability

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.680
for repeated imaging sessions.

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:55.160
In vivo tests showed sustained signal without rapid bleaching.

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:59.340
The work expands the palette of genetically encoded probes

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.500
available for longitudinal studies.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:05.620
Future iterations aim to combine multiple emission windows

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:06.760
in single animals.

